# Pinned artifacts must survive a clone BYTE-FOR-BYTE.
#
# The curated design assets and the imported reference screens are pinned by SHA-256 in
# work/implementation/DESIGN-REFERENCE-MANIFEST.json and verified by tools/design-assets-check.mjs.
# The supplied design files are LF, and this repository is used on Windows with core.autocrlf=true,
# so without these rules git checks them out as CRLF: the digest would then differ from the reviewed
# artifact on every Windows clone, and the check would pass on one machine and fail on the next.
# `-text` disables end-of-line conversion in both directions, so the bytes are the artifact.
public/assets/design/**   -text
work/design-reference/**  -text

# Migration checksums record raw bytes. Keep future checkouts stable across platforms;
# provision.mjs separately recognises the exact LF/CRLF variants of older applied files.
server/migrations/*.sql text eol=lf

# MIRROR-B1PREP-01: the imported translation bundle is pinned by SHA-256 in
# content/library-translations/README.md and re-checked by the F2 importer, for the same reason as
# the design artifacts above: on Windows with core.autocrlf=true an unconverted checkout would
# change the digest. `-text` keeps the bytes identical to the reviewed artifact on every platform.
content/library-translations/*.json -text
# MEDIA-MOUNT-01 (A12(1)): the nine listening recordings are byte-exact artifacts whose sha256 the tracked
# package pins, and their PCM duration is verified at startup. Make the binary rule explicit rather than
# relying on git's heuristic, so no checkout can ever transform them.
*.wav binary
